        </aside>

        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Is the NordicTrack EXP 7i discontinued?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              It is no longer in NordicTrack’s treadmill range: on 14 October 2026 NordicTrack’s US treadmill category listed seven models and not the EXP 7i. An old product page still loads on nordictrack.com with a price, but its price record had not changed since 2024 and the Canadian page showed it out of stock. Call NordicTrack before relying on that page.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What are the NordicTrack EXP 7i specs?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              NordicTrack lists a 20 x 55-inch belt, a 2.6 CHP motor, 0-10 mph, 0-12% incline with no decline, a 300 lb maximum user weight and a 7-inch tilting touchscreen, with a 70.8 x 34.9 x 59.7-inch footprint. Two independent reviews agree. One other source gives 3.0 CHP and 12 mph, which we treat as an error.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Can you run on a NordicTrack EXP 7i?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              You can jog on it, but it is not built for regular running. The 55-inch belt is shorter than most guidance recommends for adult runners, and the top speed is 10 mph. For running, NordicTrack’s Commercial series is the better fit.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What replaced the NordicTrack EXP 7i?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              There is no exact successor. The closest current models are the retail-only T Series 8, with an LCD and device shelf on a 60-inch belt, and the T Series 10, with a 10-inch touchscreen, both sold new with a 325 lb rating and 12 mph.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is a used NordicTrack EXP 7i worth buying?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              It can be, for a walker, if the price leaves a clear margin under a new T Series 8 and the unit passes an inspection of the belt, deck, motor, incline and screen. Assume no warranty transfers to you unless NordicTrack confirms otherwise.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

        <!-- Why trust us -->
        <section id="why-trust-us" class="ed-trust not-prose">
          <h2>Why trust Treadmill Reviews USA?</h2>
          <p>
            Every recommendation is checked against the numbers that matter for a treadmill: the maker's own
            listing and manual, at least one independent source, the warranty terms and the CPSC recall
            database. Where sources disagree we say so rather than pick a number, we say plainly when a
            machine has not been tested hands-on, and we never accept payment for a placement. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Read our review process.</a>
          </p>
